IMPORT daydate

-- Personal Injuries (Liabilities and Damages) Act 2003 (NT) -- the date arithmetic the baseline needs, kept in one small
-- module so that the daydate library is imported once. Every other module of this encoding imports this one, not daydate.
--
-- "At least 120 days from the day the proceeding was commenced have passed" (s 17K(1)(b)), "within 28 days from the day"
-- (ss 17K(3), 32J(5)) and "the day 12 months after the day" (s 32H(2)) are reckoned the plain way: the day of the event is
-- not counted, so the 28 days end on the 28th day after it, the 120 days have passed at the end of the 120th day after it,
-- and 12 months after a day is the same date 12 months on (31st of a month clamped to the month's last day). The
-- Interpretation Act 1978 rules on reckoning time (for example a last day on which an office is closed) are borrowed and
-- not encoded beyond this.

§ `Personal Injuries (Liabilities and Damages) Act 2003 -- dates`

-- A date written day, month, year (for the other modules and the cases file, which do not import daydate).
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` d m y MEANS Date d m y

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls on or before` b IF Day a AT MOST Day b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls before` b IF Day a LESS THAN Day b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls after` b IF Day a GREATER THAN Day b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls on or after` b IF Day a AT LEAST Day b

-- The number of days from a to b (for the regulative rules, whose WITHIN counts days).
GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` a `to` b MEANS Day b MINUS Day a

-- The nth day after d.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- The same date n months on (the day clamped to the last day of a shorter month).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months after` d MEANS `add months` d n

-- The later of two dates.
GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF Day a AT LEAST Day b
        THEN a
        ELSE b

-- The calendar month (1 to 12) and year of a date.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month of` d MEANS DATE_MONTH d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year of` d MEANS DATE_YEAR d
